WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.213
Week 23: Perfect Tenses and Relevant Past. report experience and recent developments connect past action to present relevance sequence prior events

2
00:00:10.213 --> 00:00:18.548
Cultural lens. Regional variation in he comido versus comí without declaring either universally preferable.

3
00:00:18.548 --> 00:00:30.619
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:42.477
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:42.477 --> 00:00:51.477
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:51.477 --> 00:01:20.380
Model language. Ya hemos completado la primera fase. — We have already completed the first phase. Todavía no han llegado los datos. — The data have not arrived yet. ¿Alguna vez has trabajado en Chile? — Have you ever worked in Chile? Cuando llamó, yo ya había enviado el informe. — When he or she called, I had already sent the report. La situación ha cambiado recientemente. — The situation has changed recently.

7
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:30.299
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
